Welcome crawlers to the seventh dungeon crawler Carl book recap where I'll be covering this inevitable ruin chapter by chapter. And do not worry, there are no spoilers outside of what happens in this book. Now, for 
those of you who've watched some of my other recap videos for Dungeon Carl, this video is going to be a little bit different. I'm going to go a little bit more into depth in some areas because this book especially when 
I first read it, I was very confused about a lot of things. It wasn't until I did my reread this year that things became more clear. And so, I really want to make sure this recap that anybody who's watching it is going 
to have a much more clear idea about what exactly is going on. And my goal, of course, with these recaps is to make sure that you get all the important details, so you get a really good understanding of what happens in 
these books chapter by chapter without going so far in depth that it takes hours upon hours to cover. That said, if you've watched some of my other recaps and you're watching this recap, it would help me out a ton to 
know what you think. This recap is probably about 50% longer per chapter than what I have done in the past. So definitely let me know in the comments whether you liked this style that's more detailed or if you preferred 
more of the fast and loose pace that I took with the other book recaps. That said, let's go ahead and get started with the prologue. The book flashes back to Carl's Christmas morning visit to the shelter, filling in the 
conversation interrupted in book six. Joff the residual speaking through Paulie tells Carl that the crawl harvests rare elements carried by the planet's population. He says those elements should feed the planet's own 
primal engine when its inhabitants die. Instead, the syndicate installs an immature AI, deprivives it of what it needs, and uses the crawl to collect those resources for the civilization at the center. At Job's request, 
Carl drinks coffee containing a neural enhancement. This connects him to the systems fail safe, giving him a way to take part in a coordinated sequence that Joff says could destroy the solar system. Paulie then offers 
his own advice shaped by his experiences living as a human. He urges Carl to hold on to compassion and keep the fail safe as a last resort, warning that a rival faction wants to destroy far more than one solar system. 
Carl is then transported back to Orin's office. In a flashback long before Carl's crawl, Porthis, the cookbook's second author, reaches the 11th floor alone. His companion, Manurva, told him to run, and he's haunted by 
having left her behind, worried by the fact that he might have been able to save her. Poris can't bring himself to go deeper into the dungeon, so he agrees to spend a hundred seasons working as a game guide in exchange 
for getting out. He hopes that the cookbook will reach someone who can continue the fight. Porthus eventually survives his indenttorship, but by the time of Carl's crawl, syndicate security list him as missing and 
wanted. Now, Carl, Donut, and Ammani arrive in Loracos on the 9inth floor with just over 32,000 crawlers remaining. They have 60 hours before the ceasefire ends. Eight enemy factions have joined together in a group 
called the block and have declared war on both the Princess Posi and Team Retribution, the MPC army led by Juicebox and Ferdinand. Donut also then accepts the MPC's offer of a truce. Carl has developed soul poisoning 
from carrying a full reserve of souls in his scavenger's daughter's patch between floors. He uses daughter's kiss on a dead shark to discharge the patch in a blast while the eye tattoo she Maria left on him remains 
unresponsive. Cascadia then explains the rules of faction wars that if a team loses if its warlord dies or an enemy holds its throne for 6 hours. Once only four teams remain, Lorocco's throne room will unlock and 
holding it long enough will ultimately decide the war. The stairwells will stay closed until the war ends or the floor is close to collapse. Donut chooses the deathbed hellcat class, gaining greater spell range and ways 
to hide herself. The adjunct Baroness of Victory urges them to start recruiting since the enemy factions can force unaffiliated crawlers into their armies. In a safe room, Donut complains about her new camouflage 
outfit, a jelly suit. We see Morai as a human this floor, though now he has a Canadian accent. His upgraded alchemy table, though, lets him examine potion ingredients and recipes, and he is preparing a potion to heal 
Mongo's missing wing. While Carl reviews their delayed rewards, Carl's Who Killed My Son quest also updates. On the previous floor, the demon prince Amayan offered to name the killer of Ember's son, Gaun, if Ember 
helped kill Amayan's three brothers. Emberest won't simply break the god's truce to carry out this deal. And Carl now has to visit Istimma's temple in Club Vanquisher and get the high cleric of the watch's permission 
for Ember to attack the brothers. The quest also requires Carl to obtain Apito's soul crystal. Now, Dona opens her reward boxes and gets construction scrolls and several new spell books. Morai stops her from reading 
them all right away. Quan's celestial cloak will upgrade four randomly selected spells from the ones Donut knows when she first puts it on, so they need to plan which spells will be in that pool. Her sponsor also sends 
her the tiara of a thousand lights and a charging pillow that transfers enchantments from other hats onto it. This will allow Donut to collect and utilize all of the buffs from her hats onto one piece of gear, although 
each original hat will lose the enchantments that it transfers. Carl also receives a separate pillow from the apothecary, though this one transfers compatible item enchantments into absorption crystals that can be used 
on a ring. Carl gives the healing potion that Morai made, restoring his burned body and missing wing. Moreai then helps Donut equip the cloak of benevolent champion over 66 hours. It will raise her lowest base stat 
constitution towards the highest one recorded when she wears it. He gives her a potion to boost her already high charisma before she puts it on, setting a much higher target for her constitution. The cloak also raises 
bat attitude to level 15 immediately. Wall of Fire, Hill Critter, and Puddle Jumper are the other three spells selected and will reach level 15 over the next 66 hours. Carl opens his own reward boxes, receiving crafting 
supplies and a merchant patch that grants access to the midnight market. He also gets the enchanted tow ring of the well balanced, which helps him keep his footing, protects him from mental control, and can 
automatically be set to use a stored potion. Carl loads a healing potion and sets it to trigger if his health falls to 2%. As soon as he equips the ring, a message says it's mind balance protection has already 
activated. Something has evidently tried to influence him, but he doesn't know what it was. After Morai examines Carl's new celestial potion, Carl drinks it and gains gloom wraith phase. and this lets him rush through 
enemies and solid objects in a ghostlike state, though being able to attack living creatures with anything he has on him as he passes through. Morai insists that he needs to practice since becoming solid again inside an 
object could kill him. Donut wants Carl to restore his hair that was burned on the FBI 4 before they begin recruiting, and he still needs to bring out Garrett, the pet Ren entrusted to him. Now, during their 
indentureship in an earlier season, we see former crawlers Dante and Justice Light are reassigned as castle guards. Justice protests that he signed a contract for non-combatant work, but Dante explains that the dungeon 
can use their classification as NPCs to make them fight new crawlers. Anyway, both men are former cookbook authors, still carrying the guilt of their own crawls. Justice says he will refuse to fight crawlers, and Dante 
has 14 seasons left before freedom. But the record at the end of the interlude reveals that he never makes it out. He is killed for refusing orders during the castle assignment. Back to present day, Carl brings out 
Garrett, the tummy ache Ren left him. And when this creature dies, it can regenerate stronger, but its level and memories reset. Garrett is now small again, and Carl has to feed him and form a new bond. Louis suggests 
renaming him Sir Rendlegore or Rend in honor of Ren. Donut worries that Carl is replacing  but Carl intends to keep his promise to care for Ren's pet. Now, Katya tries to restore Carl's hair, but the treatment calls for 
this offensive water spell that won't work inside of a safe room. And the botch treatment leaves him with long hair that keeps growing back even after it's cut. Donut gives Floren, Ellie, and Ammani senior command roles 
in the Princess Posi, while Louisie becomes Army Air General. Other members receive authority to recruit and the guild installs a doggy door connection to headquarters so they can start moving people there. Louie gets 
the guild's new elevator ready to take everyone into his aircraft hanger. And while he works the controls, Carl notices Christmas tinsel still on the guild room floor. It gets him thinking about the blurred line between 
the dungeons manufactured worlds and the real people suffering inside them. He remembers his Christmas morning encounter at the shelter and keeps what he learned about the fail safe to himself. Now, inside the hanger, 
Louis shows the group his celestial reward, the party planner, a stealth bomber that strengthens the bombs it drops and can carry Carl's customs explosives. They can board through the guild, but the plane still has to 
emerge wherever Louis parked it. The portal won't let him fly out anywhere he wants, and destroying its entrance could leave the bomber stranded until it's repaired. Floren warns that their enemies will have weapons 
designed to bring this kind of aircraft down. Carl, Donut, Louis, and Britney then head to the College of Magic to start recruiting. Donut argues with Zev about embarrassing licensed merchandise while Carl notices the 
ordinary homes and residents who will have to live through the war. They meet Arf, a Samaru dwarf who commands Lorocco's infantry. His people's history describes their search beneath the earth of the god's lost city 
which brought them to the roots of the alt tree. Arif worshiped Yasalti, the goddess who was killed on the eighth floor. Her death had left him with lower stats, increased vulnerability to other gods, and no way to 
choose another deity. Donut worries he'll connect Carl's group to what happened, but Arif welcomes them as allies. He invites them to a strategy meeting with Juicebox, who also wants to discuss marrying Louie. Arif 
leads the group down through Loracos towards its flooded castle. The city is still recovering from the flood Carl unleashed back in book four when he opened a portal from the ocean into the central market to cut off 
supplies to the enemy armies. Workers are still draining streets and repairing defenses. Now, along the way, Arif explains that some NPCs remember earlier seasons and that many of them won't return if they're killed. 
His brother was captured and tortured by architect Houston after an attempt at sabotage. Juicebox eventually infiltrated Houston's base to help end the brother's suffering. Now, Juicebox meets them in the form of a 
null, revealing herself after kissing Louis. Juicebox here is exhausted. Walking Jinx promise the NPCs protection and the ability to regenerate. they can still be killed. Juicebox also lacks a normal warlord interface 
and can't directly control Lako's defenses. She has to work through her adjunct driorm who often just ignores her. Now, Juicebox wants to move vulnerable residents outside the city to Shanty Town, but her fellow MPC 
warlord Ferdinand has stolen their food shipments. Being on the same team hasn't stopped him from causing problems. Now, Louisie admits that Juicebox also sees their marriage as a way to strengthen the alliance, 
creating a family tie between the leaders of the two armies. Britney urges Louisie to take the relationship and that responsibility seriously, and Louisie agrees to marry Juicebox. The Desperado Club's new owner is 
Hamemed, the nightworm who hired Carl and Katya to murder his wife Astred. He has barred crawlers from entering, and Carl is concerned about having another encounter with them. Now, Ferdinand arrives and Carl offers him 
Quan's enchanted bowler as a replacement to his makeshift hat in exchange for giving him authority over the settlement that Juicebox needs for her people. While Britney distracts Ferdinand with a mirror so he can admire 
himself, they secure the agreement and rename the alliance the good guys. Louisie and Juicebox marry in a small ceremony and Morai explains that the marriage is legal now, but its public confirmation comes a month 
later. Until then, the couple can anol it without penalty. Recruitment notices begin flooding in and Floren calls Carl to headquarters. In another flashback, former crawler Tippid has reached the end of his 
indenturship, but brain damage leaves him confusing his release interview with the day he abandoned his partner Horatio in the dungeon. Only one of them could use the exit key, and Tippid chose himself. The attorney 
recommends treatment Tippid can't afford from the Visroys whose members he remembers torturing crawlers in the dungeon. A support organization represented by Doctor Who might be able to help him get the care that he 
needs. Tippet eventually spends his pension and takes on debt for treatment. Returns to work for a waste management company and in the present crawl becomes the colonel of the princess posi. Now back to the present. 
Carl finds Rosita and Tippid. Remember, these are two former cookbook authors waiting at the safe room connection. These are the people whose entries have helped him stay alive and are now greeting him, though Rosetta 
recognizes the danger of she Maria's eye tattoo and asks for materials and access to Carl's crafting equipment so she can work on a treatment. Tippet explains that Porth, also known as Doctor Who, started the Crawler 
Project to help people after their contracts ended. Its work grew into a network sponsoring Carl and a campaign to end the crawl itself. When the authorities pursued its members, they put their resources in returning to 
the dungeon in joining the faction wars. And that's why 50,000 former crawlers have joined the Princess Posi where they bring experience and survival skills, but they have been reset to level 60 and only given a basic 
equipment package. On the other side, each enemy faction has received roughly 20,000 additional soldiers who get to keep their old gear. So, Carl finally has an army, but the enemy still has a huge advantage in terms of 
weapons and equipment. Returning crawlers embrace Carl as they turn the Princess Posi's wooden headquarters into a fortress, and he's overwhelmed by their support, knowing these people escaped the dungeon once and may 
now die after coming back to fight beside him. Floren uses his giant cayman to move part of the wall into place. And the guild expands beneath the stronghold with workshops and aircraft docks planned, but it won't 
provide an unlimited shelter. Also, the veterans who came back can only stay in safe rooms for a limited time before they have to go back outside. As Carl helps force open the fortress door,  rushes forward to find 
Tina, the young Allosaurus, waiting inside. Tina calls her father despite Donut's objections. Kiwi is also there, heavily pregnant and still in her original bear form that she had transformed back into during the 
butcher's masquerade. The headquarters is named the Fortress of Unyielding Power and Authority, or FUA for short. Now, as war continues, an ogre guard named Arson begins trembling and apologizing, trying to resist an 
order he's been given. And Carl realizes that Arson is covered in explosives. While Victory kills Arson before he can detonate, and Carl stores the body and the bombs, she identifies the attack as an unlawful 
assassination attempt by Sensation Entertainment, now owned by the Dream. When the AI tries to excuse it, Victory challenges that interpretation and forces an apology since someone has now tried to kill them while the 
ceasefire is still in effect. Later, Carl clears some of the windows crowding his command interface and discovers messages showing that she Maria has repeatedly tried to activate gloom wraith phase and disable his tow 
ring's protection. His new ability of mind balance has been stopping her and the repeated attempts have raised the skill to level 9. Rosetta is still working on a treatment, but for now, the ring is really what's 
keeping Shimaria from taking over Carl without his permission. Now, the adjunct victory explains that the ceasefire will be followed by a 180 hour period called the ramp up. This is where offensive magic and movement 
abilities including transportation and Carl's phasing skill will be suppressed. Ordinary guns, artillery, and stationary traps will still work. So, it's going to favor welle equipped enemy armies over more magic 
dependent forces like Carl's. With about 200,000 enemies gathering at their borders, the officers plan in trenches and minefields to hold them back. Bonnie arrives to lead the work on Louis aircraft, and Carl tries to 
shield her from the thought of killing people since she's so young. But she reminds him that outsiders keep trying to kill her, so why shouldn't she be thinking about how to kill them? Then we see Carl and Donut train 
in the forest with Chris, Jamal, and several veterans. Jamal keeps breaking his new mechanical legs when he tries to jump. He misses being able to swim and fly. And Carl keeps repairing the prototype so they can work 
out what it can handle. The group attacks a rolling battle formation. A mass of skunks moving together as a ball. Explosives break it apart and Ren feeds on the separated enemies. Killing the wizard controlling the 
skunks releases their spray all at once, leaving the group vomiting. Carl also discovers that phasing through the spray doesn't stop him from smelling it. Donut escapes into a tree and throws up while Jamal's lost sense 
of smell spares him from the nausea. Everyone survives and they collect samples for Morai. Then we see in a flashback to her own crawl. Everly, the cookbook's fifth author, trusts a sponsor's compass to guide her 
through a tower instead of cooperating with other crawlers. When she uses its final charge, an advertisement reveals that the tower was a trap designed to make the compass fail in public and promote a competing product. 
Trapped in the collapsing labyrinth with two mercenaries, Everly remembers her mother's phrase for accepting defeat, the inevitable ruin. The mercenaries keep helping her even as she gives up. Her companions remain 
beside her as the sand closes in and Everly dies on the eighth floor. Back to the present day, Morai and Rosetta prepare two treatments using modified Glorybound, the drug Katya is addicted to. Katya's dose is meant to 
take her back through the memory behind her addiction. Carl includes another ingredient intended to trap Shim Maria in her own worst memory and remove her from him. They undergo the treatments outside the safe room 
where the others will have to monitor and protect them. Carl removes the tow ring that has been blocking Shimaria with the plan to put it back on afterward. Katya says her best and worst memories are the same. And as 
the drug takes effect, she wraps her hand around Carl's arm despite warnings to keep them apart. Carl begins sensing the emotions of people nearby, especially including Katya. Now, as he's about to slip under, he sees 
an invitation to peace talks from the Lemig faction. Carl then wakes up covered in blood in the Limig castle, surrounded by dead goblins. His soul reserve is full again, and the quest to release Sheim Maria has failed. 
Commander Stockade accuses him of breaking the ceasefire. And as the adjuncts argue over who's responsible for what, Carl learns that the enemy watched his treatment and tried to summon him into a trap. And he has woken 
up in the aftermath without knowing exactly how this massacre happened. Now Carl also remembers fragments of Katya's experience, including a baby named Annie with cancer and a second spider. She Maria's husband, Aonzi. 
Katya is awake back at the hospital and believes they shut both spiders inside the memory. Carl thinks Shimaria is still trapped within him. His third eye briefly opens, confirming that fact. Now, at the hearing over 
the massacre, the adjuncts replay Stockade's peace imitation and summon Ally spell. The summons need the target's consent, so Stockade timed it for when Carl went under when she, Maria, could accept it through the 
interface. Morai explains that summoning an unconscious person normally produces a ghostlike image, preventing someone from simply abducting them. But Carl's interrupted treatment left him present in both places. The 
replay also exposes Katya's private memories. Her partner Fanar admits that he had cheated on her and Katya later sits besides the baby Annie in the hospital. Carl asked the adjuncts to stop showing this to everyone but 
they ignore him. While the hearing drags on, Prepente warns that enemy troops and artillery are moving into position. The Princess Posi's defenses aren't ready, so Carl tells Louie to prepare the party planner. The 
replay also shows how Morcai disrupted Stockade's trap. He deliberately gave Carl a dangerous wakeup potion called Shockwake, making him fully appear in the castle before Stockade was ready. And this is where Sheim 
Maria broke loose and slaughtered all the goblins. Aonzi then helped Carl close a door in the shared dream, pulling She Maria back inside him. And we see the effects of Stockade, who is still suffering from Sheim 
Maria's insanity spell. We also learned the enemy had watched Carl's treatment through outside observers who could see events ahead of the delayed broadcasts available to crawlers. Carl coordinates with Juicebox and 
Ferdinand who gets an emergency rule passed about the live feed, removing that as an advantage to other factions. The Limig faction is then penalized for the attack. But before the hearing ends, Stockade fatally injures 
himself. The system treats his death as a voluntary defeat and transfers the faction's assets to its ally, the Madness. A voluntary withdrawal also triggers an early start to the war. With a ceasefire ending 23 hours 
early, Carl is sent back to headquarters just as the first barrage hits the defenses. The story then flashes back to Christmas morning before Carl entered the ninth floor to reveal what he did after leaving the shelter. 
He asks Orin to let him revisit the dog Lightning Lou's gas station memory. There, Carl opens the containment interface which controls the equipment used to install and contain the AI inside the primal engine. The fail 
safe offers an option to override its requirements and activate it. Carl considers whether he should use it to destroy the whole solar system and everyone within it are threatened to and then thinks about donut and 
everyone else he would kill. Instead, he chooses the option of disconnect containment. Its warning says this will make the fail safe unusable and remove most of the systems controls. Carl believes it offers a way to 
hurt the syndicate without deliberately killing everyone. Back to the present, the first bombardment catches the princess posi with his defenses still unfinished. Soldiers shelter where they can while others use wind 
spells or even paper fans to disperse the incoming gas. Justice Light has fixed their throne in place, and the map now shows every team's throne, giving the armies clear targets to fight forward. Donut then assigns Carl 
a personal guard that includes Bommo and the Sledge. Staying near the person they protect gives them extra constitution, making them harder to kill. Jamal wants to come, too, but his mechanical legs keep failing. The 
army has already filled its allowance for vehicles, so Carl cannot simply give him a ride of his own and leaves him behind for repairs. When the rescued children ask to join the fighting, Carl sends them back with their 
guardians. As he and Donut head south, the souls stored during She Maria's massacre begin to poison him again. Daughter's kiss will release that power through a physical blow, but the blast is so powerful it could also 
kill nearby allies. So Carl needs to get behind the enemy's lines before so he can use it and before the poisoning can become too much for him. Now, the southern trenches are already under heavy attack, and Carl orders 
his troops to keep captured MPC soldiers unconscious so they can try to awaken and recruit them later. The Reavers send huge diseased pets called rot stickers towards the defenses, and their heavy bodies break through 
the Princess Posi shields, spreading infected remains throughout the trenches when they burst. Trans mechanical chair then unfolds into an armored fighting rig and his engineers raise earth barriers and dig passages to 
help hold the line. When an infected soldier runs through the trench, they decide to burn him to stop the disease from spreading. Victory says the attack exploits the rules and will bring penalties, but the soldiers 
will have to contain the infection themselves. Carl checks whether the restrictions on offensive magic will prevent him from using Daughter's Kiss. Because it strengthens his own physical attack, the system classifies 
it as a self-buff and allows it so he can use the blast once he reaches the enemy if the Princess Posi can get him across the ground between the armies. Colonel Boomer then prepares the bloody leeches to help lead that 
attack. He's a former crawler whose class lets him strengthen large groups of soldiers at once. Tippet tells Carl that Boomer has also spent years publicly criticizing the crawl, giving Carl an idea of about why he came 
back to fight. Now, the dream has artillery and mounted mercenaries to the south, and the prism has sent soldiers and invisible specialists from the madness are slipping into the Princess Posi's positions. Behind the 
attackers, a network of fallback trenches lead toward their support troops and commanders. If Carl's army can break into those trenches, it can keep moving through the enemy's positions. Now, the nearby Naga 
headquarters also looks like a tempting target because it appears to have very few soldiers guarding it. Carl knows that the bigger problem will be finding its warlord, which in almost all the previous seasons of 
Dungeon Collard World, that warlord tends to hide until the end of faction wars. So, for now, they just prepare to break the attack coming from the south. Louisie then begins bombing the ground between the armies, 
digging craters that will give an advantage to their soldiers and giving them somewhere to shelter. Ellie attacks the enemy's anti-air weapons so he can keep flying. And at the same time, the princess posi's mortars 
launch dazzlers which overwhelm the enemy with deafening music and flashing lights. Their own troops have earplugs and invisibility potions to help them cross through the confusion. And Carl, Donut, and also use that 
potion that surrounds them with protective air bubbles for the chemical attack planned as part of the assault. Now, some of their veterans then suggest shooting the soldiers who retreat. The donut refuses and offers 
prizes for captured enemy helmets instead. Privately, she tells Carl that she's starting to feel numb while fighting with the fear catching up to her afterwards. And Carl is starting to tremble, too, even as they keep 
preparing everyone else to advance. Now, once the bombing has opened their route, Donut gives the order, and more than 2,000 Princess Posi soldiers charge across the open ground with Carl, Donut, Ammani leading them. An 
enemy dispel strips away the advancing army's illusions and temporary shields, and the soldiers are suddenly exposed to guns and artillery far stronger than their own. Ammani protects Donut, then turns back to rescue a 
wounded soldier, while Carl releases smoke to help cover them. The survivors then reach the bomb craters and start to restore their protections. Ammani makes it there carrying the man she went back for, though the man 
is dead, and Ammani is now unconscious, barely alive herself. From this crater, Carl uses a build trench scroll and aims its construction toward the existing enemy trench. The scroll digs a passage that connects to it, 
opening a route straight into the enemy's line. Tippid has equipped other soldiers with the same scrolls, so the craters become multiple entry points without the army having to cross the last stretch above ground. They 
get inside, but there are still traps and gunfire waiting in the trenches. But Carl's soul poisoning keeps worsening as he fights his way forward. Once he reaches the enemy, he can strike and finally release that 
daughter's kiss. He does, and the blast tears apart the trench and buries Carl. He wakes about 25 seconds later, and Ammani explains that a complication of his soul poisoning made him lose consciousness while he 
released the attack. His soul reserve is now empty and his head is clearing and the enemy is retreating. Carl leaves Boomer in command of the assault and Ammani with the wounded. He and Donut board Louis plane, the 
party planner, to take advantage of the prism headquarters weak defenses. On board, Carl finds Bonnie, the changeling child, operating one of the guns. She received a scout slot while he was unconscious, making her an 
official participant in the war. As we discussed, Carl really hates the fact that children are part of this battlefield, but with the attack already in motion, he puts off confronting Louis about bringing her. Now, they 
fly low toward the prison castle, clear its few outer guards and traps, and begin to search inside. Dadia and her companions are lying there unconscious. Victory explains that the NPC scout sent ahead of them was a 
bartender with the ability called Jug of Punch. and lets him change the chemical composition of water, which he used to make Carl's incapacitating meow time potion. That potion spread throughout the castle's drinks and 
connected water supply. Because the system treated the change as crafting, the bartender could drug the occupants even though offensive magic is temporarily restricted. The story then flashes back to the fifth floor of 
Carl's Crawl, where Milk the Cookbook's sixth author is running a nearly deserted cgraphy and calligraphy guild. She took a deal to escape her dungeon, but her release from the resulting contract depends on crawlers 
using her services. Almost nobody ever comes, leaving her trapped in the guild and increasingly isolated. Miriam Prepente arrived through a secret route while fleeing guards, and Bianca's heat damages Milk's nests and 
records, and Milk considers filing a complaint that would punish the visitors. Instead, the chance to speak with crawlers again reminds her of the life she once had. So, she offers them a hidden escape out into Club 
Vanquisher and asks them to keep her guild a secret. Milk needs crawlers to use her services 333 times before she can leave, and only six visits so far have counted. She's still a long way from freedom, but she has 
chosen to help the people who find her. Back in the prison castle, Carl and Donut cannot claim victory just by walking into the throw room cuz Dinadia is still alive. And when she wakes, multiple enchantments in her 
clothing are protecting her. Carl's weapons, donuts, clockwork copies of in  himself begin to wear those defenses down. Carl then marks Dadia with his ring of divine suffering so that her death will increase his stats. 
That mark takes 30 seconds to form and he deliberately heals her to keep her alive until it is ready. As they wait, she tries to negotiate. And Carl and Donut once thought Dinadia were their friends. So hearing her talk 
this way makes her want to hurt her beyond what their plan requires and he nearly loses control. When the mark finishes forming, he forces himself to step back and he leaves Donut and there so they can kill her instead. 
So then kills Dadia, eliminating the prism and transferring its soldiers property and other assets to the princess posi. Carl's completed mark gives him five intelligence points even though made the kill. Now, an 
achievement warns that destroying Dinadia's ruling dynasty and bankrupting it could also have consequences outside the dungeon. The transfer immediately puts Carl in charge of eight mercenaries who were coming toward 
the castle with two friends from other factions. Those two are now enemies of the mercenaries that they arrived with, and Carl has ordered captured enemy mercenaries killed, but one of them, Corporal Pillbox, begs him 
to spare them, including his cousin Lockjaw, as they belong to the madness. Carl accepts their surrender and keeps lock jaw behind for a job that he has in mind. Carl's increased base stats also make the system choose 
him as party leader instead of Donut. Now Carl tells Donut that the title will not change the relationship, but Donut is more concerned about what happened with Denadia. She saw how close Carl came to losing control and 
tells him he will need her help to stay grounded. Carl knows that she is right. Now, one of the castle's surviving guards, Toyotomy, is now a princess posi soldier, too. Toyotomy explains that his edifice shield works 
on a small outpost and cannot cover the entire castle. Carl sends him to Shanty Town where the ability can do more good. Leun then reports a woman with a shopping cart who's been asking about Carl. He recognizes Agatha 
from the description and Zeb relays a warning from the council to stay away from her saying that the AI has removed the residuals protections and Agatha must need something from him. And Carl has previously been told 
the residuals are harmless. So this warning gives him another reason to doubt the competing groups trying to influence him. He suspects his own decision to free the AI from containment is involved without knowing whom 
he can trust to explain what happens next. Before leaving, Carl confines Lockjaw in the prism throne room with supplies and gets everyone else out. With only a Madness soldier occupying the room, the system starts a 
6-hour timer. If Lock Jaw can remain there, the castle and its territory will pass to the Madness's team. Carl hopes that by giving the Madness a third territory, it'll make the other enemy factions resent its growing 
share, and they'll begin to turn on one another. Carl finds a bait shop safe room near the captured castle and uses its doggy door connection to get back to the guild. He has this quick trip home from enemy territory, 
but the same network has created a route for the enemy into the princess posi's headquarters. And the entrances to these personal spaces open onto a shared corridor. Off-world soldiers with their own rooms in the same 
doggy door upgrade can enter that corridor, too, and then come through the entrance at Carl's base. And Donut realizes this mistake as the headquarters begins to come under attack. The enemy has destroyed the anti-air 
weapon and the hanger doorway, cutting off access to the aircraft parked inside, while invisible madness soldiers and reaver paratroopers begin to appear around the castle. Inside the base, Carl notices a soldier moving 
even though the casualty list says that he is dead. Valt worms are taking over the dead and using their bodies to pass as living Princess Posi soldiers. Carl forces one worm out of another corpse and kills it. Then 
orders his people to check nearby soldiers against the casualty list. The hospital is already overrun and worms inside dead mages are sabotaging the princess Posi's protections. The worms can immediately use their dead 
hosts memories and spells. They are trying to reach Lonnie, who leads the mages, maintaining the castle's protective magic so they can take his body and switch those defenses off. Rosetta searches for the possessed 
soldiers while Carl fights the attackers at the entrance. The invisible madness soldiers create a separate problem. Their concealment comes from technology, so ordinary magic cannot reveal them, although Donut can see 
them using, you know, her special goggles. Chris identifies something wrong with the princess posi soldiers as well. Focus pocus, a spell that strengthens everyone in the area, improves dexterity and concentration, but 
also makes people overstimulated and affects their judgment. Donut begins to be unusually aggressive and talkative and even the healers sound manic. Carl calls for Tina to help clear the entrance. Kiwi refuses because 
